983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2169067988">October 31, 2017</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">He’s been in all the other stories, pacing and stalking around the fringes. We’ve seen him lurking, scowling at humans, grumpy and distrustful, gorgeous and broody… Cruz is the Tiger. The loner. The dark, haunted soul who’d rather not have anything to do with anyone he doesn’t already know and trust. You don’t know much about him by this point, but what you know for sure is that he’s loyal to the bone, and if not for his brothers-in-arms, he’d probably retreat from the world completely and never look back.<br /><br />Cruz is the kind of wounded Hero a girl can’t help but fall in love with, and wish she could cuddle. The fact that he’s a Tiger in his spare time is just icing on an already irresistibly decadent, forbidden treat. He’s that sugar-laden slab of deep, dark chocolate cake sitting in the fridge that your roommate brought home yesterday: He’s calling to you in the middle of the night while she’s out for the weekend with her boyfriend and you’re home all alone with Netflix again. Come on, she doesn’t even SEE me back here! And she couldn’t possibly appreciate me like YOU can…<br /><br />Now you know you’ve got a thing for the dark and brooding guy in the group, don’t you? Tell me that you haven’t been wondering what conversations Cruz has with his inner Tiger, and I’ll call you the liar we both know you are. You have to read this book, because you’re going to find out. You’re going to learn so much more about Cruz than you thought was possible.<br /><br />The thing is, you learn about Cruz’s darkness in counterpoint to his Mate’s light. Jody is the perfect counterpoint to our Tiger’s brooding sorrow. Of all the females that we’ve seen in this series, Jody is the one who most readily accepts what would seem unexplainable to the rest of us. Her sunny disposition could coax even Cruz out of the shadows to play in sunbeams like a kitten. <br /><br />Cruz has given up on life and on love, refusing to let himself believe in anything – even Fate – but Jody follows her heart in all things, even when she shouldn’t. She doesn’t even read the fine print in her modeling contract because the offer felt like the solution to her problem at the time. She believes in things with her whole heart, and little by little, she chips away at walls around Cruz’s heart.<br /><br />There’s so much to love about Anna’s books in general, and this series in particular. I love her “Twin Moons Ranch” books, and the “Blue Moon Saloon” books are simply fantastic, but the “Lure” series have a special little place in my heart, because she weaves touches of Magnum PI into them in both obvious and unexpected ways. I grew up watching the series with my Dad religiously every week (even though my Mom insisted I was too young,) and every time I read a new “Lure” novel, I get a thrill when I find something from the show. I’m fortunate enough to have married a fan of Magnum, so he’s eager to hear what I’m squealing in excitement about, and willing to listen rather than just pretending to humor me. For just one example from this particular book, pay close attention to the car that Cruz drives… and the city his family is from. If you’re a fan of the show, you will totally get it, and you’re probably smiling right now. <br /><br />Yeah, it’s just that much fun!<br /><br />There’s lots of love, steamy scenes, and fantastic humor between Cruz and Jody (and Cruz and his Tiger!), and there’s so many touching moments, too. Just like the TV show, “Magnum PI” had more serious episodes as the series went along, so it goes with “Lure.” By now, we’re seeing more of an overarching plot going on with the Stones, and in “Lure of the Tiger,” we see more of Silas than we have before, as well. Little by little, we’re seeing more of the leader of this Pack. His story is coming next, and it feels like something really big and bad is on the horizon. <br /><br />Good thing Keiki, the Calico kitten is there to cuddle and love until Silas’ mate shows up!</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036344 L9.66834148,18.1034086 C9.31027068,18.6437214 8.696742,19 8,19 L6,19 C4.8954305,19 4,18.1045695 4,17 L4,12 C4,10.8954305 4.8954305,10 6,10 L8,10 C8.60249245,10 9.14276174,10.2664091 9.50943372,10.6878531 L9.58578644,10.6036344 L11,9.18942086 L11,6.75238209 C10.9999468,5.91477784 11.5910613,5.19356674 1