rge" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">In this, the fourth episode of the Koa Point Shifters series, Cruz is forced to face his own personal demons when he’s led astray, given a bogus lead that would have him playing target practice with the one woman who could possibly change his life. But when things suddenly don’t seem to add up, he follows his instincts and his heart. Jody has taken this modelling job without reading all of the fine print, and boy oh boy, can she see her error with that. Only its too late to do anything about it now, except follow through on her part and hope for the best. But when someone suddenly seems to be taking shots at her, with bullets no less, she’s not too sure about anything, especially why anyone would want her dead. When the most devastatingly handsome man she’s ever seen in her life comes to her rescue, asking her to trust him, and bullets are still flying, what’s a girl supposed to do? Follow her heart of course! The action these two find, all without looking, is mind boggling, and more than what either was looking for. Will it all work out in the end or will these two meet their maker first?<br />Ms. Lowe has once again given us a fast paced tale that will have you on the edge of your seat from the first page until the end. Her never ending talent to spin a complete and enchanting tale from a niggle of an idea continues with this series. If you have read any of her other series in the past, you will find a few are referenced in this one also, tying them all together in a way, yet separate. Her wonderful writing skills are always showcased and never disappoint, as I’m sure you will discover when reading this book. Now all I have to do is sit back and wait for the tale of Silas! Will he ever find his true fated mate? Or will he be destined to live out his long life solo?<br />I received a copy of this book and am voluntarily giving my honest review.<br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></se