ve done, he fights against the idea that Jody is his mate but in the case of Cruz, he fights even harder against his attraction because of his hatred for humans who killed his family but there are a lot of lessons to be learned along the way... especially when a character from the previous books makes an unexpected appearance.<br /><br />All of the previous characters in the series have fleeting appearances in this book which is a good way to catch up with what is going on in their lives but if I’m totally honest, Keiki is my absolute favourite! I love how the big, tough, macho men turn to mush whenever she’s around and the women are happy to share their mates with her.<br /><br />Unusually for me, I still don’t know who is behind all the attempts made on the mates throughout the series so am hoping that all is revealed in Silas’ story but I’m looking forward to finally finding it all out.<br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=contemporary" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">contemporary</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=dragons" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">dragons</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=hea" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">hea</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></div></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button B