ntful, irascible Tiger Shifter Cruz is charmed by easy going Surfer Jody whose motto is: 'Life is Beautiful, Love is Beautiful, You Just Have to Believe.' She was a charming addition to the mix of characters, and once again Keiki the Kitten brought out Cruz's softer, gentler, caring side.<br /><br />We got a very interesting insight into who Cruz really is, as we explored the amazing Tree House he built. It was heartwarming to see his artistic and sentimental side celebrated in the way he decorated his home with things he had created that had great personal meaning.<br /><br />I absolutely adored Cruz's inner Tiger's voice who was so very different from his personality. My favourite quote from the Book: "...which meant it was just Cruz and Silas left at home, and hell. Neither one of them was the soft and fuzzy type. I can be soft and fuzzy, his tiger insisted..."<br /><br />Highly recommend readers sign up for Anna's Newsletter to access the Bonus Scene epilogues that have heartfelt 'what happened after'. Still loving the tropical beauty of Hawaii as a backdrop for the story. Looking forward to next story to see how Silas (who has been stoic and suffering during the series), heals his heart and meets his mate. <br /><br />"I am voluntarily reviewing a book gifted to me by the author with no obligation."</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/25229672?shelf=intrigue-suspense-romance" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">intrigue-suspense-romance</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/25229672?shelf=mystical-paranormal-magical" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">mystical-paranormal-magical</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/25229672?shelf=paranormal-ani