 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2115032839">September 5, 2017</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Ms. Lowe is a stellar writer – this series, this story in particular, is a prime example!!<br /><br />What a terrific set of characters!! Our main character is tiger-shifter Cruz; tough guy, assassin, savior, keeper of kitten Keiki, and resident of a self-built treehouse. Bring on heroine Jody; pro-surfer and temporary model to earn money for her struggling family. These two characters are the main ingredients to a story which will keep you on your toes and thoroughly entertained.<br /><br />Cruz lost his family and hates humans as they were the culprit. Jody is of course human, and does not know shifters exist. Though her life has not always been easy, she believes that life is beautiful; you just have to believe. The clash of these two world outlooks is absolutely entertaining.<br /><br />A strong dose of danger, intrigue and magic combined with a growing connection between our two main characters gives us a scintillating relationship with a side serving of humor:<br />	“Why is surfing like sex? He looked at her expectantly. That, he had to hear. “When it’s good, it’s really , really good. And when it’s bad, it’s still pretty good.”<br /><br />Genuinely written at a level where you feel with the characters and become part of the action.<br />A must read!!<br /><br />*** I am voluntarily leaving my honest review of this book ***<br /></span></di