></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2113205694">September 6, 2017</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">You are missing out if you have not read this authors books.<br />Once again Ms Lowe gives us another can’t put down book. From the first line till the end we get a fantastic read that has one thinking, what next?<br />Human hating Tiger shifter Cruz is flummoxed when his tiger won’t let him kill a human woman believed to be responsible for his families murder.<br />I loved how Cruz was honest right from the start about what he was doing at the party. Him slowly finding his way to a HEA with his tiger giving him advice all the way along was so good.<br />Jody is doing a modelling assignment, which she hates but she needs to money to help her dad and sister out.<br />When Cruz saves her from another attempt on her life things really start to speed up. We get Lion shifters and Vampires as the baddies to liven things up.<br />We really don’t have too many of the group in this one as they are all off doing other things. Silas even gets called away, so when everything comes to a head, it is left up to Cruz and Jody, with the help of the Waterstone to save the day.<br />Loved having the gang all together at the end and cannot wait for Silas’ story to be told.<br />One of my favourite things about this series is that these wonderful shifters have conversations with their animal halves too. It makes them seem more real and part of the whole story.<br />This is my honest review of this book.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></sec