"text":"\u003cb\u003eChange Is Not Easy!\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis series just gets better and better. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI was excited for tiger shifter Cruz Khala to meet his mate. The brooding tiger needed just the right woman to help him overcome his painful past and help him realize that not all humans are bad. Professional surfer and part time model, Jody Monroe, was perfect for the job. Her natural inclination for enjoying life and her ability to see fun in most anything is the perfect antidote for the ever-grumpy tiger. She is like a healing balm for his wounded soul. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI loved how Silas was featured more in this book than previous books--which makes perfect sense as he will be the hero in the next book, \"Love for a Dragon.\" We learned a bit more about his background with the evil dragon shifter, Drax and about Silas's former love, Moira. The more I learned about Moira, the more I wanted to smack her. *lol*\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAs usual the story was well-written by Ms. Lowe and well narrated by Ms. Osborne. The overall story of the gemstones and how they control the elements is progressing nicely. I can’t wait to see what happens when all the gems, the shifters of Koa Point and the women are together in one spot. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI can’t wait for the next book! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eRated 1-5 stars w/ 5 being the best\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOverall: 5 stars\u003cbr /\u003ePerformance: 4 stars\u003cbr /\u003eStory: 5 stars\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eDisclosure: I received a free copy of the audible version of the book.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e(originally posted on Audible.com)","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ARNFW792RB7F\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.Z3qQSFDmpZlZ26OLlW78LQ\"}}"},"likeCount":1,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:7297738":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":7297738,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1515203180i/7297738._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":1,"textReviewsCount":143,"name":"Colleen","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/7297738-colleen","contributor":null,"id":7297738},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AUVY3KSCYOOSB":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AUVY3KSCYOOSB"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AUVY3KSCYOOSB\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.maw-alnR7rBOCGiSrrAeDA\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AUVY3KSCYOOSB","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AUVY3KSCYOOSB"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.maw-alnR7rBOCGiSrrAeDA","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.maw-alnR7rBOCGiSrrAeDA"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/7297738?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2169067988"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.jAnNYqUKXibEtU4mDfvseA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.jAnNYqUKXibEtU4mDfvseA","creator":{"__ref":"User:7297738"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1509417981977,"createdAt":1509417968422,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1509417981396,"text":"He’s been in all the other stories, pacing and stalking around the fringes. We’ve seen him lurking, scowling at humans, grumpy and distrustful, gorgeous and broody… Cruz is the Tiger. The loner. The dark, haunted soul who’d rather not have anything to do with anyone he doesn’t already know and trust. You don’t know much about him by this point, but what you know for sure is that he’s loyal to the bone, and if not for his brothers-in-arms, he’d probably retreat from the world completely and never look back.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eCruz is the kind of wounded Hero a girl can’t help but fall in love with, and wish she could cuddle. The fact that he’s a Tiger in his spare time is just icing on an already irresistibly decadent, forbidden treat. He’s that sugar-laden slab of deep, dark chocolate cake sitting in the fridge that your roommate brought home yesterday: He’s calling to you in the middle of the night while she’s out for the weekend with her boyfriend and you’re home all alone with Netflix again. Come on, she doesn’t even SEE me back here! And she couldn’t possibly appreciate me like YOU can…\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNow you know you’ve got a thing for the dark and brooding guy in the group, don’t you? Tell me that you haven’t been wondering what conversations Cruz has with his inner Tiger, and I’ll call you the liar we both know you are. You have to read this book, because you’re going to find out. You’re going to learn so much more about Cruz than you thought was possible.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe thing is, you learn about Cruz’s darkness in counterpoint to his Mate’s light. Jody is the perfect counterpoint to our Tiger’s brooding sorrow. Of all the females that we’ve seen in this series, Jody is the one who most readily accepts what would seem unexplainable to the rest of us. Her sunny disposition could coax even Cruz out of the shadows to play in sunbeams like a kitten. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eCruz has given up on life and on love, refusing to let himself believe in anything – even Fate – but Jody follows her heart in all things, even when she shouldn’t. She doesn’t even read the fine print in her modeling contract because the offer felt like the solution to her problem at the time. She believes in things with her whole heart, and little by little, she chips away at walls around Cruz’s heart.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThere’s so much to love about Anna’s books in general, and this series in particular. I love her “Twin Moons Ranch” books, and the “Blue Moon Saloon” books are simply fantastic, but the “Lure” series have a special little place in my heart, because she weaves touches of Magnum PI into them in both obvious and unexpected ways. I grew up watching the series with my Dad religiously every week (even though my Mom insisted I was too young,) and every time I read a new “Lure” novel, I get a thrill when I find something from the show. I’m fortunate enough to have married a fan of Magnum, so he’s eager to hear what I’m squealing in excitement about, and willing to listen rather than just pretending to humor me. For just one example from this particular book, pay close attention to the car that Cruz drives… and the city his family is from. If you’re a fan of the show, you will totally get it, and you’re probably smiling right now. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eYeah, it’s just that much fun!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThere’s lots of love, steamy scenes, and fantastic humor between Cruz and Jody (and Cruz and his Tiger!), and there’s so many touching moments, too. Just like the TV show, “Magnum PI” had more serious episodes as the series went along, so it goes with “Lure.” By now, we’re seeing more of an overarching plot going on with the Stones, and in “Lure of the Tiger,” we see more of Silas than we have before, as well. Little by little, we’re seeing more of the leader of this Pack. His story is coming next, and it feels like something really big and bad is on the horizon. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eGood thing Keiki, the Calico kitten is there to cuddle and love until Silas’ mate shows up!","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AUVY3KSCYOOSB\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.maw-alnR7rBOCGiSrrAeDA\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:27383555":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":2